- action(n7, "end NOK"), action(n14, "end ok"), action(n15, "end no"): Hallucinated intermediate steps. The source simply indicates that the process "comes to an end" or "is completed", without defining distinct preparatory actions named "end [status]" before the actual termination points. (SMC1)
- defines(v1, "evaluation result ok", {"NOK", "ok"}): Variable naming is semantically biased. The source refers neutrally to "the evaluation result", whereas the model embeds the specific value "ok" into the variable's identifier. (SMC6)